# Kuato

Password-gated Next.js 16 app that ranks remaining players in live [Sleeper](https://sleeper.com/) **redraft** rooms. It reads public Sleeper data. It cannot make picks.

## Scope

- In scope: snake/linear redraft, shared-password access, live board, deterministic top-5 scoring, optional LLM coach.
- Out of scope unless the task says otherwise: auction drafts, dynasty/taxi leagues, writing to Sleeper, user accounts, a database.
- Rankings must still work with no `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app/` | App Router pages and `/api/*` |
| `src/components/` | Live room, home lookup, coach panel |
| `src/lib/` | Sleeper, ADP, nflverse, scoring, AI, auth |
| `src/proxy.ts` | Session gate (Next.js 16 Proxy, not `middleware.ts`) |
| `docs/architecture.md` | Live-room data flow |

Canonical modules: `src/lib/recommend.ts` (scoring), `src/lib/live.ts` (`buildLiveState`).

## Before writing Next.js code

This is Next.js 16, not the Next.js in older training data. Read the matching guide under `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` first. Heed deprecation notices.

`AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are generated by `next dev`. Do not hand-edit them to fight the generator.

## Commands

Node 20+ and npm. Local env: copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` and set `SITE_PASSWORD`.

- `npm run lint`
- `npm run typecheck` (`next typegen && tsc --noEmit`)
- `npm test` / `npm run test:coverage` (80% statements, branches, functions, lines)

CI runs lint, typecheck, and coverage on every PR. After changing logic or UI behavior, add or update the colocated Vitest file.

## Secrets and generated junk

Never commit `.env*` (except `.env.example`), `.cache/`, coverage, or `.next/`. Keep `SITE_PASSWORD` and LLM keys server-side only. Do not paste session cookies or API keys into issues, tests, or docs.

## Docs

User-facing or scoring changes belong in `CHANGELOG.md` (`[Unreleased]`). Live-room UI changes must replace `docs/live-room.webp` (and the `docs/live-room.mp4` source).
